			title: "ZPM Circuit Assembler"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["77DE04F713EEBE61"]
			description: ["Crystal processor assemblies on a larger board make the &6Crystal Processor Computer&r, the first ZPM circuit. Several crystal assemblies for each, the ZPM assembler, and research from the station you built at LuV. ZPM hulls and the controllers of this era that ask for a circuit. Crystal assemblies come from the LuV line by ME; let the ZPM assembler draw them on demand."]
			icon: "gtceu:crystal_processor_computer"
			id: "1D98852F1AB675C2"
			rewards: [{ id: "17A9CB0334DE9233", type: "xp", xp: 120 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "556DBC5E786C7517", item: "gtceu:crystal_processor_computer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Crystal Computer"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0EFFD4E295AFAD"]
			description: ["A &6Qubit CPU Wafer&r is a wafer treated with radon so that its structure can hold a quantum state. Radon from the waste retrieval plant, which is why home comes first in this era. The qubit CPU chip, and through it the quantum mainframe. Radon is a loop: take it from the plant by ME and let the reactor return the rest."]
			icon: "gtceu:qbit_cpu_wafer"
			id: "1000B35476B6FAC2"
			rewards: [{ id: "1B15AB89BB048686", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "5A3F22E0F4B329C2", item: "gtceu:qbit_cpu_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Quantum Wafer"
			x: 2.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1000B35476B6FAC2"]
			description: ["Cut from the wafer, the &6Qubit CPU Chip&r is the part of a quantum circuit that does the counting. A cleanroom and the laser cutting GregTech asks for. The quantum mainframe. One wafer, many chips: keep a stock by ME so the assembler never waits."]
			icon: "gtceu:qbit_cpu_chip"
			id: "154A85EE43809FA1"
			rewards: [{ id: "79F1DA7C1CA9D838", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "355FAD82857C0EBB", item: "gtceu:qbit_cpu_chip", type: "item" }]
			title: "Quantum Chip"
			x: 4.0d
			y: -1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["154A85EE43809FA1", "1D98852F1AB675C2"]
			description: ["The &6Quantum Processor Mainframe&r is the biggest circuit ZPM builds, and the one the Mk2 and the research stations lean on. Quantum chips and a computer-grade board by the stack, and the ZPM assembler to put them together. ZPM machine hulls and the hatches that open the gate to UV. Make it in the assembly line from stocked parts; ME keeps the mainframes in a dedicated chest."]
			icon: "gtceu:quantum_processor_mainframe"
			id: "5353B2E6D14E53D3"
			rewards: [{ id: "31FA823ACF23F80F", type: "xp", xp: 180 }]
			shape: "gear"
			size: 1.25d
			tasks: [{ id: "79E221DF204A5F8D", item: "gtceu:quantum_processor_mainframe", type: "item" }]
			title: "Quantum Mainframe"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 0.0d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0EFFD4E295AFAD"]
			description: ["Isotopically pure silicon is grown as a &6Silicon-28 Boule&r and cut into wafers. Ordinary silicon has too much magnetic noise for what comes next. Silicon-28 from the hot cell, an EBF for the boule and a cutter. The boule is the slow part. Donor qubits, and the silicon the qubit fab asks for. The hot cell runs all day. Send its silicon to the EBF by ME and stock the wafers."]
			icon: "grindless:silicon_28_wafer"
			id: "5D07EB0A82EEE479"
			rewards: [{ id: "5D72DCF3F381B59F", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5A39D0FF474899EA", item: "grindless:silicon_28_boule", type: "item" }
				{ id: "7742C9FE252CCFBD", item: "grindless:silicon_28_wafer", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "Silicon-28"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["5D07EB0A82EEE479"]
			description: ["A single phosphorus atom in spin-free silicon holds a quantum state. The &6Donor Qubit Wafer&r is a silicon-28 wafer with them placed one at a time. The ion implanter, silicon-28 wafers and phosphorus. The qubit array, by the donor route. Implantation is slow, so run several implanters and let ME collect the wafers."]
			icon: "grindless:donor_qubit_wafer"
			id: "1D7FE3922B3DBF22"
			rewards: [{ id: "16561E6518BA9165", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "394DF0F6F19CC29B", item: "grindless:donor_qubit_wafer", type: "item" }]
			title: "Donor Qubits"
			x: 4.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["7B0EFFD4E295AFAD"]
			description: ["A nitrogen atom next to a gap in diamond is a qubit that works warm. The &6NV Diamond Chip&r is a doped diamond plate with them placed in it. Nitrogen-doped plates from the diamond lattice fab, then the ion implanter. The qubit array, by the slower diamond route. The doped plate is the slow step; give the fab its own nitrogen feed."]
			icon: "grindless:nv_diamond_chip"
			id: "5F0C09AC946B3ECA"
			rewards: [{ id: "3F118BCA0B5E4A1F", type: "xp", xp: 100 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [
				{ id: "5E012EA6434CDC82", item: "grindless:nitrogen_doped_cvd_plate", type: "item" }
				{ id: "5E94DFBC293D0FAA", item: "grindless:nv_diamond_chip", type: "item" }
			]
			title: "NV Diamond"
			x: 2.0d
			y: 4.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["1D7FE3922B3DBF22", "5F0C09AC946B3ECA"]
			description: ["Qubits only hold their state when almost nothing is moving. The &6Cryostat Casing&r keeps the fab that cold. Aerogel and gold-plated copper for the casing, and a helium-3 and helium-4 mixture to run the cold. The qubit fab, and every cryogenic hall that comes after. The mixture is not consumed: top it up with a little helium-3 by ME."]
			icon: "grindless:cryostat_casing"
			id: "119B62380F5F76FC"
			rewards: [{ id: "1FAA0F12448553D4", type: "xp", xp: 80 }]
			shape: "hexagon"
			size: 1.0d
			tasks: [{ id: "7B831BE9E559C9AB", item: "grindless:cryostat_casing", type: "item" }]
			title: "Millikelvin"
			x: 6.0d
			y: 1.5d
		}
		{
			dependencies: ["119B62380F5F76FC"]
			description: ["A &6Qubit Array&r stands in for a stack of circuits in the computation parts our alternative recipes build. Donor wafers or NV chips, and the cold charge the qubit fab runs on. The computation components for the research station, at a fraction of the circuits. Keep a stock by ME; the fab is slow and the components draw them by the handful."]
			icon: "grindless:qubit_array"
			id: "5E3D46F05A5DC030"
